        "instruction": {
          "title": "4. Molecular vs Electron-Domain Geometry",
          "description": "Now let's replace bonding domains with lone pairs. The underlying electron-domain geometry stays tetrahedral, but the visible molecular geometry changes to trigonal pyramidal (Ammonia) and then bent (Water)."
